A||N||2||rockcrawl|| how to determine final drive ratio of 4spd auto||||5||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||11-01-2000||04:24 PM||||I have 3 TH440-T4 transmissions, one Olds, two Caddy. One of them will be installed in my '87 GT with a rebuilt 2.8. Is there any way I can tell what the final drive ratio is without tearing them appart? Can the dealer tell me? Are they all the same or did differnt cars use different ratios?<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-01-2000||04:58 PM||||Not sure with GM. Ford used to have a tag on it's rears and if you ran the tag numbers thru the dealer they could tell what gears were in it. I know there's a tag on the GM's but I don't know how useful it is.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||11-01-2000||08:03 PM||||If you know what car they are from than just look up the cars specifications and you will find the information you are looking for. I have a 440-T4 transmission in my old 89 Bonneville and the axle ratio is 2.93. The newer Bonnevilles have 3.08 92 and up.||||reg||1
